ecent fundamentals environment keep this from being Safe R, but the challenger trails clearly.", "watch": "Any fresh independent polling or major outside spending for Knickerbocker could narrow the race into Lean R territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 77 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Mike Turner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Ohio's 10th District, anchored in Dayton, leans Republican by about four points and has re-elected Mike Turner repeatedly. Turner enters the general with a large financial advantage over Democrat Kristina Knickerbocker, who has raised a modest sum for a targeted race. A Libertarian candidate also appears on the ballot.\n\nRaters overwhelmingly call the race Likely Republican, with one rating it Safe R and one Lean R. The only polls, conducted in July by Democratic sponsors, showed Turner ahead by seven to eight points, though they are now dated. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-seven chance. National Democrats have advertised here, suggesting they see some opening, but the combined evidence points to a Turner win with modest but real uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1787, "margin": -5.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1387, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1203, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.155, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.119, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1452, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1169, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1457, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1476, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1448, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1049, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1332, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1454, "margin": -6.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_de